**Theorem 4.3.** Consider the multivariate linear regression model (4.1) under the assumption ORT or, equivalently, the sub-Gaussian matrix model (4.2). Then, the singular value thresholding estimator \(\hat{\Theta}_{\mathrm{svt}}\) with threshold

\[
2 \tau = 8 \sigma \sqrt{\frac{r \log(12)(d \lor T)}{n}} + 4 \sigma \sqrt{\frac{2 \log(1/\delta)}{n}}, \tag{4.3}
\]

satisfies

\[
\frac{1}{n} \| X \hat{\Theta}_{\mathrm{svt}} - X \Theta^{*} \|_{F}^{2} = \frac{1}{n} \| \hat{\Theta}_{\mathrm{svt}} - \Theta^{*} \|_{F}^{2}
\leq 144 \, \mathrm{rank}(\Theta^{*}) \, \tau^{2} = C \sigma^{2} \, \mathrm{rank}(\Theta^{*}) \frac{d \lor T + \log(1/\delta)}{n}
\]

with probability at least \(1 - \delta\).
